/-!
# H10--H14 frontier with symmetry-generated actual zero modes

This façade combines the strongest current H11 route with the Noether kernel
bridge.  The six non-Robin Hessians are the actual Candidate-A chart Hessians,
the Robin block is the H10 GHY second Fréchet derivative, and named zero modes
are generated by invariance of the same augmented action gradient along their
one-parameter orbits.

Consequently no field of the terminal packet states `H v = 0`.  Kernel
membership is proved, the canonical finite-span splitting is constructed, and
the global Gårding inequality excludes hidden modes before H12 is invoked.
-/

namespace JanusFormal
namespace P0EFTJanusProgramPGlobalHessianCanonicalSixSymmetryOrbitFrontier4D

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 12800000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 6400000

noncomputable section

open Set Topology MeasureTheory
open scoped Manifold ContDiff InnerProductSpace
open P0EFTJanusMappingTorusQuotient
open P0EFTJanusMappingTorusSmoothAtlasFrontier
